<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # My Personal Success Story – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Personal Success Story</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Successful</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td colspan="3" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td colspan="4" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Summarize technical instructions clearly. Communication: Facilitate diverse group discussions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can summarize technical instructions on budgeting and lead group activities to practice these steps (e.g., "Let's create a group budget for a school trip. First, we list our expenses. Then, we compare costs and agree on how much each team member will contribute.")</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can facilitate group discussions on personal goals using supportive body language to encourage engagement (e.g., nods and gestures to encourage classmates to share their future goals).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can clarify technical terms in English for diverse groups (e.g., "Budgeting means planning your money, like how you decide to save five dollars every month for your future goals.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f0f8ff;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students participate in a "Explain It Simply" activity. The teacher displays three different simple concepts related to success (e.g., "Setting a goal," "Community service," "Financial planning"). Students choose one and have 30 seconds to explain it in their own words to a partner, pretending their partner knows nothing about it. This activates prior knowledge about the theme "How I Am Successful" and introduces the concept of clarifying information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher projects a short, slightly technical paragraph about "Effective Savings Strategies" (e.g., "To build long-term savings, an essential strategy is diversifying your investment portfolio. This involves allocating funds across various assets like stocks, bonds, and real estate, reducing overall risk."). The teacher models summarizing it clearly: "This means don't put all your money in one place. Spread your money across different types of investments like stocks or property to be safer." The teacher also models stressing content words in the summary: "Spread your MONEY across DIFFERENT types of INVESTMENTS."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main idea of the original paragraph?" (To check understanding of the source text).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the purpose of my simplified explanation?" (To check understanding of summarization/clarification).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Personal Success Story"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informational text (genre: technical instructions, register: informative, format: blog post excerpt or official guide section) titled "Four Key Steps to a Successful Personal Budget." The text includes sections on "Tracking Expenses," "Setting Realistic Goals," "Creating a Savings Plan," and "Reviewing and Adjusting." It uses vocabulary like <i>finances, savings, investment, strategies, growth, opportunities</i>, and grammar structures such as the present perfect ("I have successfully tracked my expenses for months") and first conditional ("If you regularly review your budget, you will achieve your financial goals faster").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpretive Communication: Understanding and summarizing the main points and key details of a structured informational text containing technical instructions related to financial planning for future success.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the text individually.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the primary purpose of this article?" (Multiple choice: a) To describe past achievements, b) To provide steps for budgeting, c) To compare investment options). "What is one general strategy mentioned for financial growth?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match each of the four key steps (e.g., "Tracking Expenses") to a brief description (e.g., "Knowing where your money goes").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice summarizing technical instructions, clarifying vocabulary (<i>finances, investment, strategy</i>), and using present perfect for achievements ("I have saved"), future continuous for long-term goals ("I will be managing"), and first conditional for future success ("If I invest, I will build"). Pronunciation focus on stressing content words (e.g., "Set REALISTIC goals").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Summarization and Term Clarification:</b> In pairs, students receive sentence strips, each containing a complex sentence from the "Four Key Steps to a Successful Personal Budget" text. For example: "Prudent financial management involves meticulous documentation of all monetary transactions to ascertain areas for potential expenditure reduction." Students must rephrase it simply, writing it down. They also identify one technical term and provide a simpler English explanation (e.g., "meticulous documentation" means "careful record keeping"). The teacher circulates, checking for accurate rephrasing and appropriate vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Facilitating Discussion Prompts:</b> Students work in small groups (3-4). Each group receives a specific budgeting step (e.g., "Setting Realistic Goals"). They prepare two questions to lead a brief discussion based on this step, incorporating target grammar (e.g., "What future goals will you be pursuing that require careful planning?" - future continuous; "If you set a clear goal, what opportunities will you achieve?" - first conditional). They also prepare one clarification for a key term from their step (e.g., clarifying "realistic goals"). They practice leading these mini-discussions within their groups, ensuring everyone contributes.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Mediation - Explaining Personal Strategies:</b> Students interview a partner about their current or desired financial strategies for a future goal, using pragmatic phrases for respectful discussion ("How has saving helped you build your future plans so far?"). Each student then summarizes their partner's strategy to another pair, clarifying any terms their partner used and modeling natural stress on content words.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Personal Success Story"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Presentation and Facilitated Discussion based on the "Financial Planning Infographic" project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students, in their project groups, present their "Financial Planning Infographic" on saving for future goals. Each group member takes turns leading a section of the presentation, focusing on mediating the information to the class. They must:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Summarize technical instructions:</b> Clearly explain 2-3 key budgeting or saving steps from their infographic to the audience (e.g., "First, you must initiate a careful record of your expenses, which means simply writing down everything you spend."). Use target grammar like the present perfect ("We have included steps that have proven successful...") and future continuous ("If you follow these, you will be effectively managing your finances in no time!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarify terms:</b> Explain any potentially complex vocabulary from their infographic (e.g., "investment," "return on investment," "diversification") using simpler English, as if for a peer who is new to financial planning.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Facilitate discussion:</b> Lead a brief (2-3 minute) Q&A or discussion with the class, encouraging classmates to share their own personal goals and saving strategies ("What skills would you like to develop for your future goals?"). The presenter uses supportive body language (nods, open gestures) to encourage engagement and ensures all voices are heard respectfully.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation focus:</b> Consciously stress content words when presenting and clarifying.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min (2-3 min per group)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment:</b> Teacher uses an observation checklist to assess students' mediation skills during their infographic presentations. Peers provide feedback using a simplified rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students (individually within their groups) present a section of their "Financial Planning Infographic" project, demonstrating their ability to summarize technical instructions clearly, facilitate a brief discussion on goals/strategies, and clarify any complex terms from their infographic.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of Summary:</b> Can accurately and clearly summarize technical budgeting instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary & Grammar:</b> Appropriate and varied use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>investment, strategies, growth</i>) and grammar (present perfect, future continuous, first conditional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarification of Terms:</b> Effectively explains technical terms using simpler English.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Discussion Facilitation:</b> Engages peers, encourages participation, and ensures respectful dialogue.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible Pronunciation:</b> Stresses content words for natural rhythm and clarity.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new strategy I learned for explaining complex ideas was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I am confident in clarifying terms like _____ because I can explain it as..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has this project on financial planning improved my understanding of personal goals and provided opportunities for future success?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific mediation skill (summarizing, clarifying, or facilitating) do I feel most successful with, and which one would I like to improve for my future career-related projects?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The group presentations showed strong collaborative interaction, with students effectively using the first conditional to discuss future success strategies. Most students demonstrated good clarity when summarizing, but some still struggled with reducing stress on auxiliary verbs, making their speech sound less natural. Adjustments for future lessons will include more explicit pronunciation drills focusing on sentence rhythm within longer explanations, and perhaps providing more diverse authentic technical texts for summarization practice. The integration of the infographic project provided an excellent real-world application of mediation skills.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> As this is Lesson 5, it concludes the theme "How I Am Successful" and the "My Personal Success Story" scenario, integrating all four skills through mediation. The next lesson will introduce a new theme and scenario, building upon the collaborative and presentation skills developed here, potentially involving a new 21st-century project that requires similar mediation of information.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>